# Pass Handler — build-time configuration
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# These are OAuth *public client* IDs. They are not secrets — a public client
# has no client secret by design, which is why we use PKCE. They are kept out
# of the repository anyway so that each person who builds the app points it at
# their own Google Cloud project.
#
# With both values unset the app still builds and runs: it stays local-only and
# the Settings screen reports that Google Drive is not configured.
#
# See docs/google-oauth-setup.md for how to obtain these.

# OAuth client of type "Desktop app" in the `pass handler` Google Cloud project.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID_DESKTOP=

# OAuth client of type "Android" in the same project. Requires the package name
# `com.passhandler.app` plus the SHA-1 of the signing key. Debug and release
# keys have different fingerprints and need separate clients — set this to the
# debug client while developing and swap it for the release client when you cut
# a build to hand out.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID_ANDROID=
